Read elk-rs's clone registry without a shared lock

ElkReflect looks up the function that clones a property's default under
one global mutex, and every read of an unset property does so; with
frames laid out in parallel the layout threads spend most of their time
contending for it.

License: EPL-2.0 (elk-rs v0.11.0+rs.2)

